WEBVTT

00:00:04.052 --> 00:00:08.581
Welcome to leyoNET. In this video you learn where to find what.

00:00:08.581 --> 00:00:12.536
In the middle is the canvas. This is where you build your network.

00:00:12.536 --> 00:00:18.953
On the left are the devices: end devices, servers, switches, routers, Wi-Fi and more.

00:00:18.953 --> 00:00:22.418
Below is the task with its learning goals.

00:00:22.418 --> 00:00:25.958
On the right you see the properties of the selected device.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:30.509
At the very top are the menus. All functions can be found here too.

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:37.469
Use the Datei (File) menu to open and save projects. Ctrl+S saves as well.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:43.203
The Werkzeuge (Tools) menu holds the exercise catalogue and the IP calculator.

00:00:43.203 --> 00:00:47.003
In the toolbar: select and draw cables.

00:00:47.003 --> 00:00:52.146
Clicked the wrong thing? Undo takes back the last step (Ctrl+Z).

00:00:52.146 --> 00:00:57.002
This is the project name. Your file will have the same name.

00:00:57.002 --> 00:01:01.877
leyoNET has two modes. In design mode you build and configure.

00:01:01.877 --> 00:01:07.118
In simulation mode your network really runs. Switch with the M key.

00:01:07.118 --> 00:01:10.694
Let's look at a finished example: demo networks.

00:01:10.694 --> 00:01:15.002
Choose “ARP und Ping im LAN” and click Vorführen (present).

00:01:15.002 --> 00:01:20.013
The simulation starts and PC 1 pings another PC.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:25.293
This is the PC's desktop: command line, web browser and e-mail.

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:29.272
We minimise the desktop and look at the packets.

00:01:29.272 --> 00:01:34.869
At the bottom is the packet list. Every row is a packet that was sent.

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:40.529
Clicking a device shows on the right what it currently knows, e.g. its address.

00:01:40.529 --> 00:01:47.696
Not sure? F1 opens the help. It matches what you are doing.

00:01:47.696 --> 00:01:53.625
And Ctrl+K searches every function. Just type what you need.

00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:57.995
That was the overview. In the next video you build your first network.
